 /*
$diary has a "page" for each day(since the diary was started) and each page has a number of entries with time, text, opinion/comment, importance and effects
so you access entry text with $diary[logdaynumber][entrynumber][$logpars.text]
.time is simply $time
.text is the diary entry that describes what exactly happened in 1st person
.importance allows filtering out simply moving around and such and is used to decide how to colour the text
.comment is a string the player can input, set $diaryprompts to 1 or 2 to be asked for comment whenever an event is done
.opinion (could be about) how you feel about an event and how you've chosen to rationalise it or just the default comment
.written is to indicate if you have sat down and actually written the entry(if that matters)
.stats lists most stat changes like money since the last time log widget was used.

to make this work time.twee has a thing that pushes a new day/page into existence at the start of each day, it also reports the date and stat changes of the day
other than that and this there are some widgets at the bottom of widgets.twee and initStory and Start2() from init.twee are used to initialize everything.
And finally nearly all events would ideally have the following bit near the end:

<<set $logprep to "">>
<<log $logprep 3>>
<<logopinion "">>

1st "" being filled with diary entry and 3 beig the importance of event
logopinion could have various opinions about the event split into different $args[] with $diaryprompts 2 or 3 events ask you to pick between them whenever they end

for more complex events usingg $logprep to change entry text based on choices made earlier is useful:

<<set $logprep to "">>
<<set $logprep to $logprep+"">>
<<set $logprep to ""+$logprep>>

<<log $logprep 3>>
<<logopinion "">>

note using variable inside the string ie "$logprep blah" will make it update when $logprep changes while using $logprep+"blah" doesn't do that

Also if it's really necessary <<logadd>> and <<logupdateeffect>> can also be used to change the last entry
for example if you want to have logopinion but there's still a choice with all options ending the event and putting you on street or something.


$logextra will cause <<log>> to (sneakily) add another entry after the current one if it's anything other than ""


<<awarenesswords "some person">>  can be used to set variables like $aw_rapesx to be something like "rapes some person"
<<endcombat>> will do <<awarenesswords "me">> setting $aw_xx to awareness based variation of "rape me", "molest me" or "have sex with me" based on $rapeavoid and $sexavoid
ie.:
<<pronouns>>
<<endcombat>>
<<set $logprep to $He+" "+$aw_xedx"+".">>
<<log $logprep 3>>
<<logopinion "">>

Can have results like "He raped me." and "She touched me weirdly."
<<pronouns>> sets various variables like _he _him _his to match $pronoun since widgets like <<he>> don't work when building a string(the result changes with pronoun).



*/


:: Simple Diary[nobr]

<<for _i, _day range $diary>>
  <br>
  <<for _j, _entry range $diary[_i]>>
    _entry[$logpars.text]
    _entry[$logpars.comment]
    
    <<print JSON.stringify(_entry[$logpars.stats])>>
    <br>
  <</for>>
<</for>>

:: Diary Stringified [nobr]

<<print JSON.stringify($diary)>>

:: Write Diary [nobr]

You sit down and start writing to your diary.
<<if $eventlog is undefined>>
  <<set $eventlog to $diary>>
<</if>>

<<logcount>>
<<if _unresolved.traumagain gte 10>>
<</if>>
<<if $eventlog.length-1 gt 1>>
It's been <<print 0+$days-$diarywriteday>> days since your last entry it takes you a moment to recall everything that happened.
<</if>>
<br>

<<showdiaryentry 0 0>>
<<showlogentry>>
How do you want to write this entry? (carefully written entries about bad events may make you recall them but  
  little effect but also won't help much)
Quickly(0:01)
Normally(0:02)
Carefully(0:05) 
Stop



<<if $rationalisation.deserve isnot undefined>>
  I deserved that.
<<elseif $rationalisation.holy isnot undefined>>
  <<if _resistsuccess isnot 1>>
    My blessings belong to everyone.
  <<else>>
    They didn't deserve my blessing.
  <</if>>
<<elseif $rationalisation.learn isnot undefined>>
  At least I learned something
<<elseif $rationalisation.need isnot undefined>>
  They probably needed that more than I was 
<<elseif $rationalisation.kind isnot undefined>>
  Hopefully they are happier after that. 
<<elseif $rationalisation.polite isnot undefined>>
  <<if _resistsuccess isnot 1>>
    It would have been rude to deny them.
  <<else>>
    It was rude to deny them.
  <</if>>
<<elseif $rationalisation.weak isnot undefined>>
  <<if _resistsuccess isnot 1>>
    I was too weak, it's only right for strong to rule over weak.
  <<else>>
    I proved myself stronger than them.
  <</if>>

<</if>>



Things are better now

[[Next|Write Diary]]
<<link [[Done]]>><<return>><</link>>

